{"sections":[{"slug":"Arthur–Selberg迹公式","section":{"metadata":{"slug":{"Plain":"Arthur–Selberg迹公式"},"ext":{"Plain":"md"},"title":{"Plain":"“Arthur–Selberg <span lang=\"zh\">迹公式</span>”"},"taxon":{"Plain":"<span lang=\"zh\">百科</span>. "},"author":{"Lazy":[{"Local":{"url":"/SimplicialCat","text":"SimplicialCat"}}]},"page-title":{"Plain":"“Arthur–Selberg 迹公式”"},"data-taxon":{"Plain":"百科"}},"content":{"Lazy":[{"Plain":"\n<blockquote>\n<p>A key tool in the study of automorphic forms is the Arthur-Selberg trace formula, which expressed <strong>spectral quantities</strong> (traces on representations) in terms of <strong>geometric quantities</strong> (orbital integrals). — <span lang=\"zh\">恽之伟</span>, Hitchin-type moduli spaces in automorphic representation theory</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>"},{"Local":{"url":"/Hitchin模叠","text":"Hitchin <span lang=\"zh\">模叠</span>"}},{"Plain":"</p>\n"}]}}}]}